   "user": "O_oNevermore",
   "message": "I think people respond negatively because your intent is very \"in your face\"\n\nyou aren't just saying something you are proud about what you are doing with the knowledge that it would ruffle feathers\n\nit's kinda like you are pressing the \"leave a hate comment\" button in the mind of the audience \n\nall of your questions are shiboleths, the people that agree with you are taking a hit because they like you (the hit is they look like morons because your questions are designed to make the ingroup look moronic to the outgroup)\n\nI find the dynamic repulsive personally, not condemning, just saying, it is dissonant with my aesthetic (which is nothing to write home about itself so...)\n\nanyway, there are some people I work with that are easy to meme, everyone instinctively memes them as being uncool or idk what the word is, they are kinda just easy targets, and we didn't come together and conspire \"ah this guy sucks let's meme him\" it just happens cuz their aesthetic is wrecked\n\nand ofc they then get treated that way and then if they can't change their aesthetic they adopt this \"in your face\" attitude because they are successful regardless of being a joke to people",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-29T14:07:55.911000+00:00",
